-- Passage rg8-comparing-texts-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('d115c877-71e0-53e1-805f-4be8d2cf48a6', 'rg8-comparing-texts-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-comparing-texts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Choosing the Ground$q$, $q$Text 1: Fox Chooses the Path (a tale)

Antelope was the fastest animal on the plain, and he never let anyone forget it. Each morning he raced past the others and laughed as dust settled on their fur.

One day Fox said, "I will race you to the river." The animals gasped. Antelope's legs were twice as long as Fox's whole body.

"Agreed," said Antelope, "and you may even choose the path."

Fox chose the path through the bramble wood, where the branches grew low and thick. Antelope's long legs caught on every vine, and his horns tangled in the branches. Fox slipped under the thorns like water under a door and reached the river first.

When Antelope finally stumbled out, Fox was drinking calmly. "You are faster," Fox said. "But I know where to run."

Text 2: Low Post (a story)

Mina was the shortest player on the Eastfield Hawks, a full head below the center on the other team. In the first quarter, she tried to shoot over the taller girls. Three of her shots were blocked straight back at her.

At the timeout, Coach Osei knelt beside her. "Stop playing their game," he said. "Where are you faster than they are?"

Mina thought about it. The tall players were slow to bend down. So she stopped shooting from the outside. She dribbled low, close to the floor, and cut through the crowded lane where long arms got in each other's way. She slipped past two defenders and made an easy layup.

By the fourth quarter, the other coach was shouting at his players to stay low. They could not. Mina finished with fourteen points.$q$, 'draft')
