-- Passage rg8-comparing-texts-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('04b8ab5b-ddb1-5825-b9ab-a64ebaa5c02f', 'rg8-comparing-texts-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-comparing-texts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$A Kindness Returned$q$, $q$Text 1: The Sparrow in the Net (a tale)

A girl named Teodora walked to market each morning past the fishing nets drying on the shore. One morning she heard frantic chirping. A sparrow had flown into a net and wrapped its wings in the cords.

Teodora was already late. The baker would not save bread for anyone who came after the bells. Still, she knelt in the sand and untangled the cords one by one until the sparrow shot into the sky.

She missed the bread that day and went home hungry.

A month later, Teodora was gathering shells far down the beach when a sparrow landed on her shoulder and pecked at her ear. It flew toward the town, then back, then toward the town again. She followed it, puzzled. Minutes after she reached the road, a wall of rain swept over the beach where she had been standing.

Text 2: Combination (a poem)

First day, a new kid at the locker next to mine,
spinning the dial the wrong way, again,
while the clock above us counted down.
I could have walked past. Most people did.
I showed him: right, left, right,
and we were both late to science.

In March, my project fell apart
the night before the fair, wires loose,
the little motor silent in my hands.
A message lit up my phone:
You need help? I'm good with motors.

He came over with a box of parts.
We worked until the motor hummed.
Neither of us said a word
about a locker in September,
but I think we both remembered.$q$, 'draft')
